{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-fork-dev-origins-1790900465602", :event/time "2026-10-02T00:21:05.602Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "fork-dev-origins", :parent nil, :card-type "epic", :type "task-created", :write-id "1790900465598-0.2czmco9mqytq0wisg31", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "EPIC: develop on riatzukiza forks; orgs receive promotions and run ops", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/epic-develop-on-riatzukiza-forks-orgs-receive-promotions-and-run-ops--origins.md", :status "incoming", :body "# EPIC: Development happens on riatzukiza forks; the orgs only receive promotions and run ops\n\n## Outcome\n\nEvery Foresight submodule from `open-hax` or `octave-commons` has a `riatzukiza` fork that is its development origin. Feature PRs are opened, reviewed and merged on the fork. Code reaches the org repository only through a promotion: the fork's `main` is pushed to an org branch, and an in-org PR runs the org's secrets, required checks and deploy gates. Ops-as-code in `open-hax/services` deploys from the org repositories.\n\n## Context\n\n- Observed 2026-10-01 from each repository's CodeRabbit review footer: the personal account `riatzukiza/*` is on Essentials at 5 reviews per hour. `open-hax` and `octave-commons` are on the free OSS program at 1 review per hour.\n- CodeRabbit's knowledge base: a personal subscription \"does not extend to organization repositories\". Each org needs its own subscription.\n- In this session, the hourly org limit was the main wall-clock cost of the review loop (open-hax/foresight#120, octave-commons/shx#2).\n- User decisions (2026-10-01):\n  - promotion is a push to an org branch plus an in-org PR, not a cross-fork PR, because fork PRs run without the org's secrets and the eta-mu review gate needs them;\n  - Foresight's `.gitmodules` points at the forks;\n  - every org submodule moves.\n- GitHub constraints (observed 2026-10-01):\n  - An account can hold one fork per network. `riatzukiza/mojomast-opencode` already forks `anomalyco/opencode`, the network of `open-hax/opencode`.\n  - `riatzukiza/uxx` forks `shuv1337/uxx`, so the dev fork of `open-hax/uxx` needs another name.\n  - `riatzukiza/axxium` is only a transfer redirect to `open-hax/axxium`.\n\n## The core identity\n\nThe fork is where work is reviewed; the org is where reviewed work becomes operational.\n\n## Children\n\n- `dev-origin-map` — the fork↔org map as validated data in `.cljc` — **hard blocker for the rest**\n- `create-dev-forks` — create the forks and enable Actions — needs `dev-origin-map`\n- `fork-review-setup` — CodeRabbit, Codex, branch protection and auto-merge on every fork — needs `create-dev-forks`\n- `foresight-submodules-to-forks` — `.gitmodules`, project model and local remotes point at the forks — needs `create-dev-forks`\n- `pr-flow-promotion` — a `promote` stage and command in pr-flow — needs `dev-origin-map`\n- `org-ops-only` — org `main` accepts only promotion branches; documented in services — needs `pr-flow-promotion`\n- `fork-org-drift-check` — org `main` must always be an ancestor of fork `main` — needs `dev-origin-map`\n\n## Definition of done\n\nA feature PR on a `riatzukiza` fork is reviewed by CodeRabbit under the personal plan and merged there. It then reaches the org repository through `pr.cljs promote`, and the in-org PR passes the org's required checks. This is shown end to end on at least one repository, and every other repository is configured the same way.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nnbb scripts/project.clj validate\nnbb -cp ~/.agents/skills/pr-flow/scripts ~/.agents/skills/pr-flow/scripts/pr.cljs flow promote\n```\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Moving or archiving the org repositories, which stay canonical for ops.\n- Paid CodeRabbit subscriptions for the orgs."}, :causal/root "2251aad7-6ebd-4926-b71f-71a13b75da60"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-dev-origin-map-1790900465820", :event/time "2026-10-02T00:21:05.820Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "dev-origin-map", :parent "fork-dev-origins", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1790900465819-0.qjktgtt0chhkx20d6", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Record the fork-org map as validated data", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/record-the-fork-org-map-as-validated-data-igin-map.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Record the fork↔org map as validated data\n\n## Outcome\n\n`config/dev-origins.edn` lists, for each org submodule, its dev origin (`riatzukiza/<name>`) and its org upstream. A pure `.cljc` law validates the file, and `nbb scripts/project.clj validate` fails when a submodule has no entry, an entry names no submodule, two entries share a fork, or a fork name breaks GitHub's one-fork-per-network rule as recorded.\n\n## Context\n\nEvery other story reads this map. Known exceptions (observed 2026-10-01):\n- `open-hax/opencode` uses the existing `riatzukiza/mojomast-opencode`.\n- `open-hax/uxx` needs a non-`uxx` name, because `riatzukiza/uxx` forks `shuv1337/uxx`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] GIVEN `.gitmodules` and `config/dev-origins.edn` WHEN validated THEN every `open-hax`/`octave-commons` submodule has exactly one entry with `:dev/origin` and `:org/upstream`.\n- [ ] GIVEN an entry whose `:org/upstream` is not a declared submodule WHEN validated THEN it fails, naming the entry.\n- [ ] GIVEN two entries with the same `:dev/origin` WHEN validated THEN it fails.\n- [ ] VERIFY: the law lives in `src/foresight/*.cljc`, with no I/O.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nnbb scripts/project.clj validate\nnbb -cp scripts:test test/project_test.cljs\nclj-kondo --lint scripts test src\n```\n\n## Anti-patterns\n\n- Do not derive fork names at runtime from repository names; exceptions must be explicit data."}, :causal/root "b7ef7674-e9a4-454a-96e0-f316d804ff22"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-create-dev-forks-1790900466031", :event/time "2026-10-02T00:21:06.031Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "create-dev-forks", :parent "fork-dev-origins", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1790900466030-0.7dn0nocmvyh5vulugkt", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Create the riatzukiza dev forks", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/create-the-riatzukiza-dev-forks-ev-forks.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Create the riatzukiza dev forks\n\n## Outcome\n\nEvery entry in `config/dev-origins.edn` exists on GitHub as a fork of its org upstream, with Actions enabled. A script run with `--dry-run` reports nothing left to create.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] GIVEN the map WHEN the script runs THEN each missing fork is created with `gh repo fork <org>/<name> --fork-name <dev name> --clone=false` and existing ones are left unchanged.\n- [ ] GIVEN a created fork THEN its Actions are enabled and its `main` matches the org `main` SHA at creation time.\n- [ ] VERIFY: `--dry-run` after the run reports zero actions.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nnbb scripts/dev_origins.clj check\n```\n\n## Anti-patterns\n\n- Never delete or rename an existing `riatzukiza` repository; report collisions instead.\n- No secrets are copied to the forks; deploy credentials stay in the orgs."}, :causal/root "10d5f921-f9ca-411b-9736-cc49493f5dc1"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-fork-review-setup-1790900466249", :event/time "2026-10-02T00:21:06.249Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "fork-review-setup", :parent "fork-dev-origins", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1790900466248-0.lfhi5umkpejwvj34fo9", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Configure review and merge protection on every fork", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/configure-review-and-merge-protection-on-every-fork-ew-setup.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Configure review and merge protection on every fork\n\n## Outcome\n\nEvery fork has the CodeRabbit and Codex apps installed. Its `main` is protected with required checks, required conversation resolution and auto-merge, matching its org upstream's checks where those checks don't need org secrets.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] GIVEN a fork WHEN a probe PR is opened THEN CodeRabbit reviews it, and its footer reports the personal plan (Essentials, 5 per hour).\n- [ ] GIVEN each fork THEN `gh api repos/riatzukiza/<name>/branches/main/protection` shows required checks plus `required_conversation_resolution: true`, and `allow_auto_merge` is true.\n- [ ] VERIFY: no required check depends on a secret the fork does not have, since a required check that can never pass blocks every merge.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nnbb scripts/dev_origins.clj check --protection\n```"}, :causal/root "0adc5f66-df9f-4c73-a66b-b74a41be1d6b"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-foresight-submodules-to-forks-1790900466467", :event/time "2026-10-02T00:21:06.467Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "foresight-submodules-to-forks", :parent "fork-dev-origins", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1790900466466-0.qvomj4unqee5iehd8q", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Point Foresight's submodules and local checkouts at the forks", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/point-foresight-s-submodules-and-local-checkouts-at-the-forks-to-forks.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Point Foresight's submodules and local checkouts at the forks\n\n## Outcome\n\n`.gitmodules` and `src/foresight/project.cljc` (`:source/url`, plus a new `:source/upstream`) name the forks. Each local checkout has `origin` set to the fork and `upstream` set to the org. Project validation and the workspace tests pass.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] GIVEN a fresh `git clone --recurse-submodules` WHEN it completes THEN every pinned SHA is fetched from its fork.\n- [ ] GIVEN each local submodule checkout WHEN `git remote -v` runs THEN `origin` is the fork and `upstream` is the org.\n- [ ] VERIFY: `nbb scripts/project.clj validate` and both root test files pass with the new URLs.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nnbb scripts/project.clj validate\nnbb -cp scripts:test test/project_test.cljs\nnbb -cp scripts:test test/workspace_test.cljs\n```\n\n## Anti-patterns\n\n- Do not rewrite a submodule's history or force-push; only remotes and URLs change."}, :causal/root "9ce70a5f-25b2-473c-824c-fbb525f5d74b"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-pr-flow-promotion-1790900466689", :event/time "2026-10-02T00:21:06.689Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "pr-flow-promotion", :parent "fork-dev-origins", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1790900466688-0.00n8zss0nnvseww06myvj", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Add a promote stage to pr-flow", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/add-a-promote-stage-to-pr-flow-romotion.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Add a promote stage to pr-flow\n\n## Outcome\n\n`pr-flow/flow.edn` gains a `:promote` state after `:merged`. `pr.cljs promote <dev-repo>` reads the map, then:\n1. pushes the fork's `main` SHA to the org branch `promote/<short-sha>`;\n2. opens an in-org PR into the org's `main`;\n3. hands that PR to the existing merge gate with the org's reviewers.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] GIVEN fork `main` at SHA X WHEN `promote` runs THEN the org has branch `promote/<X7>` at exactly X, and an open PR from it into the org's `main`.\n- [ ] GIVEN the org's `main` is not an ancestor of X WHEN `promote` runs THEN it refuses with a drift error (see `fork-org-drift-check`).\n- [ ] GIVEN `flow.edn` WHEN `test_law.cljs` runs THEN the new state is reachable from `:merged`, and every named skill exists.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nnbb -cp ~/.agents/skills/pr-flow/scripts ~/.agents/skills/pr-flow/scripts/test_law.cljs\n```\n\n## Anti-patterns\n\n- Not a cross-fork PR: those run without the org's secrets.\n- Never force-push the org's `main`."}, :causal/root "f88a6d0a-ada2-4080-aa7e-d3799659525d"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-org-ops-only-1790900466911", :event/time "2026-10-02T00:21:06.911Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "org-ops-only", :parent "fork-dev-origins", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1790900466909-0.dolmmjy9vsvnq0uq3e4", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Make org repositories promotion-only and document the split", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/make-org-repositories-promotion-only-and-document-the-split-ops-only.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Make org repositories promotion-only and document the split\n\n## Outcome\n\nEach org repository's `main` accepts changes only through `promote/*` PRs. `open-hax/services` documents that ops-as-code deploys from org repositories, and that development happens on the forks.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] GIVEN an org repository WHEN a PR from a non-`promote/*` branch targets `main` THEN a required check fails with a message naming the fork.\n- [ ] VERIFY: `open-hax/services` `README.md` names the fork/org split and links to `config/dev-origins.edn`."}, :causal/root "f28ba622-3e75-4c84-ba95-9a04d7ce9f9f"}
{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-fork-org-drift-check-1790900467158", :event/time "2026-10-02T00:21:07.158Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "fork-org-drift-check", :parent "fork-dev-origins", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1790900467148-0.mkdkg6rvecmh4g0sljt", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Detect fork/org drift", :source-path "/home/err/spaces/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/detect-fork-org-drift-ft-check.md", :status "incoming", :body "# Detect fork/org drift\n\n## Outcome\n\nA check reports any repository where the org's `main` is not an ancestor of the fork's `main`, such as a hotfix landed directly on the org. It runs in `nbb scripts/project.clj validate --remote` and before every `promote`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] GIVEN the org `main` equal to or behind the fork `main` THEN the check passes.\n- [ ] GIVEN a commit on the org `main` that is missing from the fork THEN the check fails, names the repository and the SHAs, and suggests merging `upstream/main` into the fork.\n- [ ] VERIFY: the ancestry decision is a pure function over SHAs and parent lists, tested without network access.\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\nnbb -cp scripts:test test/project_test.cljs\n```"}, :causal/root "ad91d5bb-351d-4aeb-bf34-4ea66bd922d4"}
