{:event/type "kanban.task-created", :event/id "kanban-7f7b6b5b-2df1-4e52-a167-8e631ca598e4-476d238e-4051-4bf8-8673-11b3f2c0fab4", :event/time "2026-10-15T01:54:46.988Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "7f7b6b5b-2df1-4e52-a167-8e631ca598e4", :dependency ["2f4421ee-2e48-405e-96d2-fee1a5597ff2"], :parent "8bcaa0f3-37ec-44e2-8f20-4798dfc4b795", :card-type "task", :type "task-created", :write-id "1792029286944-0.r09oxzi6iavu3td731", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :title "Persist the separate deterministic mood transition and replay interface", :source-path "/home/err/.codex/worktrees/cephalon-kernel-selection/foresight/docs/agile/kanban/persist-the-separate-deterministic-mood-transition-and-replay-interface-1ca598e4.md", :status "incoming", :epic "63a0e4ff-353f-4c90-ab8a-7241d958d54c", :body "## Context\n\nInitial Incoming planning child of existing finite mood integration parent `8bcaa0f3-37ec-44e2-8f20-4798dfc4b795`, within the accepted B1/B2/B3 scope. This splits existing work, not new behavior or prerequisite scope. Points are provisional for independent estimate/reuse/aggregation review before lawful Ready; the parent's recorded5 is non-additive aggregate history.\n\n## Scope\n\nUse the named completion boundary and shared resource/receipt/authority rules in ../../notes/2026-10-14-cephalon-finite-delivery-plan.md. Katamorph/Axxium/Clio retain canonical authority. A completed earlier interface does not require its successor to run.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nComplete the larger mood story, invent accepted mood axes, bypass Rheos/review/authority, introduce another persistence kernel or clock, change credentials/provider/paid use, or call source fixtures live proof.\n\n## Outcome\n\nDeliver an independently qualified deterministic mood state/transition and persistence/readback interface; runtime appraisal and actual maker integration complete in the separate consumer child.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Review the separate schema/dimensions/ranges/uncertainty, baseline/decay, causal encounter/field/time inputs, model/configuration/seed identity and typed output. Historical diagnostic axes/keyword counters are not accepted dimensions. Consume a validated appraisal as data, without provider calls or clocks in the pure transition.\n2. A selected admitted encounter/appraisal causes the reviewed expected dimension change. Persist prior/next state and causal identities with actual stored scope/expected revisions, then independently read back that exact resulting revision. Model no-op cannot pass the positive; missing/invalid input explicitly refuses or follows the reviewed validated fallback.\n3. Freeze prior state, validated appraisal, elapsed time, configuration and seed. Replay identical state/trace without external mutation or duplicate persistence. Duplicate/out-of-order/conflict/failed/uncertain persistence has explicit outcomes and cannot lose or multiply changes; inspect reuse of the existing Clio application port before adding a storage authority.\n4. Quiet positive-elapsed input from a nonbaseline persisted mood, without message/appraisal/provider call, produces the reviewed expected decay, persists and independently reads back. Identical replay matches; duplicate delivery cannot decay twice. Zero elapsed has its distinct no-op case.\n5. Supply typed immutable mood revision/readback/trace to the consumer. This packet completes with bounded pure/storage fixtures and source qualification; it does not require provider-failure handling, production turn preparation or served B2 observation.\n\n## Verification\n\nPlanning qualification and full-graph native readiness precede RED/GREEN. Execute meaningful causal RED before portable domain and owning outer-adapter GREEN; no model calls/clocks in the pure transition. Append actual commands, source/configuration identities, results and evidence hashes after every finished job to the existing owning receipt ledger. Corrections append. Before full snapshots/installations measure free space; below20GiB allocate no extra full copy. At most3 expensive checkout/snapshot jobs across this goal. Preserve unique source/refs/locks/evidence and prior failures.\n\n## Risks\n\nStale/revoked authority, unknown dimensions or mapping, duplicate/conflicting state, incomplete readback and confusing source proof with served consumption remain explicit refusals.\n\nLicense: GPL-3.0-or-later."}, :causal/root "d5d8838a-328f-4e35-899c-269985096d42"}
