ected matching and no forbidden retained disclosure; public outcomes retain their authorized independent readback. If protected verification or safe evidence is unavailable, refuse outcome proof and reinforcement. No publication replay.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1792032169382-0.xaszd0r6tqq00xnupd", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "d5f0e9e6-b42a-4d16-aa05-6e9d817f2ef6"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-2f4421ee-2e48-405e-96d2-fee1a5597ff2-5c01fc15-0fc1-4378-bd01-2f9f9d2138e4", :event/time "2026-10-15T03:16:01.100Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "2f4421ee-2e48-405e-96d2-fee1a5597ff2", :text "Verified current planning correction: Atomic authorization consumes an Axxium-owned current decision and its policy/grant version through the qualified Axxium interface, bound to actual stored principal, action, resource and permitted scope. Validate that Axxium decision/version through commit under its qualified admission/fencing seam, not just an OpenPlanner cached grants/policy snapshot or a locally minted version. Reload actual owner inputs and refuse revocation/mismatch/unsupported commit protection before any graph/field/effect component commits. Use the actual qualified Axxium shape/field names at the adapter; this declaration invents no competing authorization implementation. A fixture with stale local grants but current Axxium denial must write nothing.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1792034161098-0.9lklx7iiiwrfxhe5jz", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "ed2e7b60-c651-45d2-8e18-196b6161e5a3"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-d68344c4-f18b-4b96-8585-bd8f7ac7c6a2-58a97798-6f4d-47d6-9b4a-9844b739323e", :event/time "2026-10-15T03:16:02.315Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "d68344c4-f18b-4b96-8585-bd8f7ac7c6a2", :text "Verified current planning correction: Checkpoint state includes the actual producing compiled-artifact SHA256, build-qualification identity and exact launch-profile identity/digest, alongside kernel/config/numeric revisions. Bind these to independently verified qualified producing source/build/runtime evidence and include them in the canonical checkpoint hash. Restore independently verifies the actual currently loaded artifact/build/launch qualification and requires equality with that producing identity before causal use; same revision labels alone cannot pass. Missing producer fields or a byte-different artifact/build/launch identity refuses unchanged state. No silent migration, copied producer label or new snapshot hash can qualify a different producing executable; a separate reviewed migration would be required outside this finite same-artifact replay proof.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1792034162312-0.zj4x45zllr6z3duspg", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "136dadd0-2192-4889-9ccb-849032cd30a2"}
{:event/type "kanban.comment", :event/id "kanban-ba078119-482c-49dc-bd18-c2dfcaad9024-b881bc76-2b04-490b-9ce0-c2b77808ec57", :event/time "2026-10-15T03:16:03.432Z", :session/id "kanban", :delivery/mode "tell", :payload {:task-id "ba078119-482c-49dc-bd18-c2dfcaad9024", :text "Verified current planning correction: The tuple of end-boundary step ID and canonical unordered pair is a deterministic contact/domain key within the admitted kernel history, not native event identity. Pure kernel observations are data. The outward adapter maps that key, immutable source/history and ownership to the qualified canonical Clio event envelope; Clio owns emitted event identity, causal stream and idempotency admission. Retain the actual admitted Clio event reference beside the domain key so replay recovers the same event/effect without reminting. Never deduplicate or authorize a downstream effect solely with the tuple or implement a local event-identity scheme; unsupported Clio admission refuses outward effects. Split/catch-up/restore fixtures verify the same domain observations and canonical admitted event/effect references.", :source "cli", :agent "eta-mu", :write-id "1792034163429-0.j3t1gtoswvmhuhi111", :type "comment"}, :causal/root "557cca32-1e70-4c85-b0f5-4044e8ff47ca"}
